  "body": "## What is wrong\n\n`assets/machines/tormach-770mx-microarc4.mch:13` states an A travel of -360..360.\nThe refusal at `assets/posts/tormach.cps:723` uses this value.\nmkinney posted a PathPilot Hub reading on PR #2386 after the merge. In that reading, A jogged to 1484.663 and no alarm occurred.\nIf that reading is correct, the post refuses legal programs on the shipped machine file.\n\nPR #2386 did not set the travel value. It added the refusal that uses it.\n\n## Source\n\nThe read-only Opus review of the merged PR #2386:\nhttps://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/pull/2386#issuecomment-6972209368\n\nThe review read the diff only. It did not build and it ran no test.\n\n## Open question\n\nThe correct A travel of the microARC 4 on PathPilot is not confirmed by a public Tormach document in this issue.\nFind that source first. Do not change the value on one Hub reading only.\n\n## Done when\n\n- The machine file states the A travel that a public Tormach source or a recorded machine reading supports, and names that source.\n- A test pins that a wrapped A program inside the true travel posts, and that a program outside it is refused.\n\n## Workaround\n\nEdit the A travel in a copy of the machine file.\n",
